# q2-usbtrace trace format (docs/internals.md#usb-tracer), built from a device log for test/unit/test_usb_fsm.py.
# Source: q2-replug2-state.log, 2026-11-17, build p32b (before the blank and the settle), a pin sample every 0.5 s,
# as transcribed in test/fw/test_usb_otg.py LOGGED and docs/internals.md#otg-host-power: each run is an unplug from a
# computer, PD18 low after it, and stock's bus power "in the next pass (within 0.53 s every time)", so otg-on is put
# 0.53 s into the low (an upper bound). The log has no online field: 1 is assumed while the computer's cable is in,
# 0 after. After stock's otg-on the pins are stock's doing (its power holds PD18 low and masks the cable), so the
# replay is judged only up to that line; each run ends there.
602.900000 start
602.900000 s PD17=0 PD18=1 PC20=0 on=1
607.900000 s PD17=1 on=0
608.970000 s PD18=0
609.500000 s PC20=1 PD17=0
617.250000 start
617.250000 s PD17=0 PD18=1 PC20=0 on=1
622.250000 s PD17=1 on=0
623.320000 s PD18=0
623.850000 s PC20=1 PD17=0
637.940000 start
637.940000 s PD17=0 PD18=1 PC20=0 on=1
642.940000 s PD17=1 on=0
644.530000 s PD18=0
645.060000 s PC20=1 PD17=0
650.130000 start
650.130000 s PD17=0 PD18=1 PC20=0 on=1
655.130000 s PD17=1 on=0
658.310000 s PD18=0
658.840000 s PC20=1 PD17=0
660.200000 start
660.200000 s PD17=0 PD18=1 PC20=0 on=1
665.200000 s PD17=1 on=0
665.730000 s PD18=0
666.260000 s PC20=1 PD17=0
